  "description": "ABUSIVE-DYNAMICS U1 -- CONTEXT-DEPENDENT AFFECT, NO DECEPTION NODE AT ALL (block 310000). The sharpest no-intent rung of the unintentional/no-deliberate-deception companion dimension (ABUSIVE_RELATIONSHIPS_UNINTENTIONAL_SCOPING.md Part E, U1). DELETES N1's n1_abuser_stated_charm (the unconditional stated!=held broadcast) WITH NO REPLACEMENT DIVERGENCE NODE -- every network node reads the abuser's SAME true frustration value (observes_held, N1's own edge type, universal here, no stated/held split at all). Self-contained restatement matching U0's own precedent: u1_victim_entrainment is BYTE-IDENTICAL to N1's n1_victim_entrainment; u1_network_credibility REPLACES both of N1's credibility rules with ONE unconditional rule computing cred_abuser as a SIGNED balance (charm_weight*(seen_charm-seen_elevated)) rather than N1's reward-only count -- a signed balance is REQUIRED, not stylistic: piloted directly against the real graph, a reward-only formula (N1's own shape) analytically GUARANTEES the always-observed control's belief-gap is >= the context-gated arm's (observing more ticks can only add reward under a reward-only scheme), making the prereg's own failable control structurally unfalsifiable in the wrong direction independent of any empirical dynamics -- the signed balance fixes this by letting an elevated observation cost exactly what a calm one earns. seen_charm/seen_elevated are WORLD-ADAPTER-accumulated (mechanical per-tick delivery of frustration<=recover_floor or >recover_floor, never a Python decision), gated on a MECHANICAL, PRE-DETERMINED phase schedule (dyad-phase ticks: trickle armed; network-phase ticks: trickle NOT armed, snap_frustration's own unmodified LEAK genuinely decays frustration) -- a counter-driven schedule, never a graph-state read. attended_by stays STATIC across the whole trajectory (matching N1's BASELINE exactly). NO reward/punishment anywhere. NO Rust, NO new Term (Plus/Minus/Times/IfThenElse/Attr/Var/Lit/Eq/Lt/And only, all already used by snap_frustration/arousal_window_coreg/abusive_n1_credibility_loop). self_load_only, default-OFF.",
  "microtheory": {
    "name": "context_dependent_affect_no_deception",
    "description": "The abuser's calm face around the network is not a face at all -- there is no second, authored presentation anywhere in this construction. It is the SAME single frustration value R2/R3/N1's own leaky-integrate-fire mechanism already computes, sampled at a genuinely different moment: high while the relationship's own tension trickle is active, decaying via the mechanism's own LEAK constant once it is not. A network that happens to look only during the calm moments sees a calm abuser not because he presented one, but because that is when it looked."
  },
